{"id": "tesla-2026-11-14-021", "date": "2026-11-14", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 46, "weekday": "Sat"}, "entities": {"companies": ["tesla"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Tesla Cybercab’s autonomy agreement is insane: $299/mo or it doesn’t move", "content": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://electrek.co/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2026/02/Tesla-Cybercab-hero.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Tesla has posted the agreement that comes with its $29,990 Cybercab, and it’s even worse than the order page suggested. The two-seater can’t move without a $299 monthly “Autonomy Subscription” that Tesla can reprice with a month’s notice, suspend for a week, or cut off entirely.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-para", "sources": [{"name": "electrek", "url": "https://electrek.co/2026/11/14/tesla-cybercab-autonomy-subscription-agreement-terms/", "type": "rss"}]}
